#!RuleTest
#test CT-RUN-1 expect=skipped domain=VS
#note CTD-2 row T2 — blank field, no define, the Trial Summary states CDISC CT 2023-12-15 but the store holds only 2024-09-27: a TS-derived package is NAMED, so the run ABORTS naming it and its TS row (D3), with the same escape hatch as the define (fill the CT Packages field).
#ct-available sdtmct-2024-09-27
#expect-abort "The Trial Summary (TS) states controlled-terminology package 'sdtmct-2023-12-15' (TSVCDREF \"CDISC CT\", TSVCDVER \"2023-12-15\")"
dataset VS
col VSSTAT type=Char
---
BOGUS
---

dataset TS
col STUDYID  type=Char
col TSPARMCD type=Char
col TSVAL    type=Char
col TSVCDREF type=Char
col TSVCDVER type=Char
---
S1 | TCNTRL | PLACEBO | CDISC CT | 2023-12-15
---
